<!-- question: 3 -->
  <question type="stack">
    <name><text>PDE Basics - Q3: Simple PDE Solve</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the PDE:</p>
<p>\[ \frac{\partial u}{\partial t} = 0 \]</p>
<p>subject to the initial condition \( u(x, 0) = {@ic_expr@} \).</p>
<p>\( u(x, t) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Since \(\frac{\partial u}{\partial t} = 0\), \(u\) does not depend on \(t\), so \(u(x,t) = f(x)\).</p>
<p>Applying the initial condition: \(f(x) = {@ic_expr@}\).</p>
<p>Therefore \(u(x,t) = {@ic_expr@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
